{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nClosing a ticket can freeze every other agent's writes to the tickets store for minutes. The\nclose's post-write tail calls `_compact_on_close` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:92`,\ncalled at `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:526`), which runs compaction;\n`compact_txn._compact_locked` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:328`) takes the ONE store\nwrite lock at `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:340` and holds it for the whole fold — read,\nreduce, authorship ledger, snapshot write, retire renames, and the git add/commit.\n\nMeasured on this host: closing `271c-e88f-3220-4c9b` held `.ticket-write.lock.d` from 20:35:52\nuntil its `ticket: COMPACT` commit (72ff0358f7) at 20:49:45 — 13m53s, one continuous hold.\nThree other closes the same hour held 2m27s, 2m27s and 2m41s. Concurrent agents then burn\ntheir acquire budget and lose writes.\n\nNothing bounds that hold. Inside the store lock every git call goes through `compact_txn._git`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:41`) -> `gitutil.run_git_write`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:472`) -> `_with_index_lock_retry`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:339`), which opens with `_store_git_op_lock`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:365`) — a SECOND per-store advisory flock. Its budgets stack\ninside the held store lock: `_STORE_GIT_LOCK_WAIT_S = 30.0`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:209`), `_INDEX_LOCK_ATTEMPTS = 10`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:125`), each attempt up to `_TRANSIENT_HEAD_ATTEMPTS = 3`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:418`) children bounded by `_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:468`). `_compact_locked`'s own `timeout=30, attempts=2` bounds\nonly ACQUIRING the store lock, never HOLDING it. The 7084 stand-aside probe\n(`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:121`) cannot help the closing process, which\nreleased the lock ~3 seconds earlier so the store always reads free.\n\n## Approach\nTake compaction off the close path entirely: delete `_compact_on_close` and its call site so a\nclose ends after signing, the force-close audit comment and scratch cleanup. This alone\nrestores close lock-holds to the seconds the other three acquisitions already take (sidecar\nappend, `txn.transition_core`, SIGNATURE append), because compaction is the only unbounded\nholder in the tail.\n\nThis is safe because compaction is OPTIONAL housekeeping, not a correctness step — the\nfunction's own docstring already states it (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:92`: a\nskip is a NO-OP for correctness, the raw events stay live and the next compaction folds them),\nand `_compact_on_close` already skips itself whenever the lock is busy. An unfolded event log\nis completely valid; the reducer replays it. So removing the trigger changes performance and\nstore size, never stored state.\n\nCompaction itself is NOT removed: `rebar compact <id>` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:65`)\nstays exactly as it is, and the scheduled out-of-band sweep that becomes the standing trigger\nis the follow-up ticket that `depends_on` this one. Landing this first is deliberate: it is\nthe whole P0 fix, it is small enough to review as one change, and it unblocks every stalled\nagent today rather than after the sweep is built. The interim cost is that ticket event logs\ngrow until the sweep lands — accepted, bounded by that follow-up, and recoverable at any time\nwith a manual `rebar compact`.\n\nDeleting the function also removes the only production caller of\n`rebar._store.lock.write_lock_is_busy` (`src/rebar/_store/lock.py:214`). That function STAYS:\nit is a documented store-API probe with its own test suite\n(`tests/unit/test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py`), so this is not dead code to remove here.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` — delete `_compact_on_close` and its call site;\n  drop the now-unused local imports it owned.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_on_close_skip_7084.py` — delete: every test in it\n  exercises the removed function.\n- `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` — drop the two `monkeypatch.setattr(transition_close,\n  \"_compact_on_close\", ...)` lines (`:285`, `:313`) that patch the removed name.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py` — new regression test.\n- `docs/concurrency.md` — update the compact-on-close description to say compaction is\n  out-of-band.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — record the behaviour change.\n\n## Testing\n- A close of a ticket whose event count is far above the compaction threshold writes NO\n  SNAPSHOT, retires NO source, and produces no `ticket: COMPACT` commit — the events stay live\n  and the ticket still reduces to the same state as before the close.\n- A background sampler polling `.ticket-write.lock.d` every 20ms across a full close observes\n  the lock only in short bursts, and never across a span that includes a compaction fold; the\n  close's own `ticket: STATUS` commit still lands.\n- `rebar compact <id>` on that same ticket still folds it normally afterwards, proving\n  compaction is intact and only its trigger was removed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Closing a ticket performs no compaction — a test asserts that after\n      `transition <id> in_progress closed` the ticket dir contains no `-SNAPSHOT.json`, no\n      `*.retired` source, and the tracker log has no `ticket: COMPACT <id>` commit.\n- [x] The close still produces its normal artifacts — the same test asserts the `ticket: STATUS`\n      commit landed and the reduced ticket status is `closed`.\n- [x] Compaction still works when invoked directly — a test runs `rebar compact <id>` on the\n      just-closed ticket and asserts the SNAPSHOT is written and the sources are retired.\n- [x] `_compact_on_close` no longer exists — a grep of `src/rebar` for the symbol returns no\n      match, and no test patches it.\n- [x] `docs/concurrency.md` no longer describes compaction as running on close, and the full\n      local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786603416936825001,"uuid":"ff3a6c47-ac9c-4ffe-926f-af135ac32a7a"}